%% DM26-0670

%% A signed admin action, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/authority-model.md). The only way to provision an account, grant or revoke: the unsigned topics were removed.
%% PolicyUpdate is a variant the handler refuses, NotYetSupported: policy goes by signed document (policy_update_enforcement). What a revocation does next is general/revocation.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Administrator
    participant Tool as polar-admin-grant
    participant Obs as Credentials observer<br/>(low trust)
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Con as Credentials agent<br/>(consumer)
    participant Ledger as Ledger
    participant Graph as Neo4j<br/>(a projection)

    Admin->>Tool: grant, revoke or provision-account, with --cert, --key, --observer-url
    Tool->>Tool: sign the action with the admin's key. The certificate only signs: it is not the transport
    Tool->>Obs: POST /admin-action, plain HTTP, with a 120 s timeout
    Obs-)Bk: credentials-admin-action-requests
    Bk-)Con: delivered, through the request gate, judged as the observer

    Con->>Con: the author by serial in the ledger: UnknownAuthor, AuthorRevoked
    Con->>Con: the signature: BadSignature. The payload: MalformedPayload
    Con->>Con: the capability, from the ledger's record and never the certificate: MissingCapability
    Con->>Con: a bootstrap certificate provisions once: BootstrapCertificateSpent
    Con->>Con: by action: NotYetSupported, ReservedUsername, AccountAlreadyExists,<br/>AccountAlreadyPending. Provisioning mints the account's id
    Con->>Ledger: RecordAdminAction
    alt its payload hash was seen before
        Ledger-->>Con: Replay
    else
        Ledger->>Ledger: append AdminActionRecorded, hash-chained and synced.<br/>The grant, revocation or account follows from it in the fold
        Ledger--)Graph: the projection, fire and forget: the reply never waits for it
    end
    Con-)Bk: Recorded, Refused or Failed on credentials-admin-action-replies
    Bk-)Obs: the reply
    Obs-->>Tool: its HTTP status
    Tool-->>Admin: exit 0 only on Recorded

    Note over Admin,Tool: A grant to an IdP identity has to name the claim cert-issuer<br/>extracts for that issuer, found by hand in the IdP. No code touches<br/>an IdP here, and a provisioned account needs none of it:<br/>its names come from the provisioning record
